  "body": "### What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nMoves multimodal forward metadata computation (mrope `rope_deltas`, ViT `cu_seqlens` /\r\n`max_seqlen`, `grid_thw` lists) out of `Model.forward` / `ViT.forward` and into the\r\ndata pipeline (CPU dataloader workers, off the GPU critical path).\r\n\r\nThe motivation is the follow-up tracked in PR #764: the runtime ViT/Model forwards\r\nderived this metadata from GPU tensors, each derivation costing one or more implicit\r\nhost↔device CUDA syncs. Computing it CPU-side eliminates those syncs — the model just\r\nconsumes precomputed CPU ints / CPU tensors that the trainer batches onto the device.\r\n\r\n**The derivation is model-owned, not collator-owned.** Addressing review feedback\r\n(Coach257): the ViT metadata formula is Qwen-VL-family-specific (it depends on model\r\nconfig the collator does not have), so it is *not* a framework-wide multimodal\r\ncontract. Each wired model exposes the derivation as a picklable hook — mirroring\r\n`get_position_id_func` — and the collator stays generic: it packs / SP-pads /\r\nSP-slices and then *invokes* the model's hook.\r\n\r\nEvery consumer site keeps a **runtime fallback**: when `multimodal_metadata` is\r\nabsent the model derives the metadata in-forward exactly as before. Behavior-\r\nequivalent and opt-in.\r\n\r\n### Checklist Before Starting\r\n\r\n- Follow-up to #764.\r\n- PR title follows `[{modules}] {type}: {description}` format.\r\n\r\n### Test\r\n\r\nCPU-side:\r\n\r\n- `pytest tests/data/test_mm_metadata.py` — **10/10 PASSED**. Covers the generic\r\n  helpers, the collator → `metadata_collate_func` hook handoff, and hook\r\n  picklability (the multiprocessing-worker contract).\r\n- Verified the generated `collate_multimodal_metadata` reproduces the prior\r\n  `batch_vit_metadata` + `extend_vit_metadata_for_sp_pad` + `bundle_multimodal_metadata`\r\n  output (temporal-unroll cu_seqlens + SP-pad tail).\r\n- `python -m veomni.patchgen.check_patchgen` — all generated files in sync.\r\n- `make quality` — passes.\r\n\r\nGPU-side (validated on an A100 worker):\r\n\r\n- `pytest tests/models/test_model_forward_no_implicit_sync.py` — sync gate,\r\n  **6/6 PASSED**. `_ALLOWED_SYNCS` line numbers re-synced after the\r\n  `collate_multimodal_metadata` helper shifted the generated files (pure line\r\n  drift; observed-sync counts unchanged).\r\n- `pytest tests/models/test_models_logits_equal_v5.py -k qwen` — **26/26 PASSED**,\r\n  no numeric regression across the qwen2/qwen3 lineage.\r\n\r\n### API and Usage Example\r\n\r\nNo public API change. Internal additions:\r\n\r\n- New optional `multimodal_metadata: dict | None` kwarg on the patched `Model.forward`\r\n  of the wired models; `vit_*` kwargs on the patched `ViT.forward`. All optional, all\r\n  with runtime fallback.\r\n- Two new patchgen-added model methods: `get_metadata_collate_func()` (returns a\r\n  picklable hook the collator invokes after SP padding) and `get_extra_collate_infos()`\r\n  (omni only — declares the audio collate rules).\r\n- `MainCollator` gains an optional `metadata_collate_func` param.\r\n\r\nThe full producer/consumer contract is documented in\r\n`.agents/knowledge/multimodal_metadata.md`.\r\n\r\n### Design & Code Changes\r\n\r\n**Generic collator protocol (`veomni/data/`):**\r\n\r\n- `data_collator.py` — `MainCollator` carries an optional `metadata_collate_func`;\r\n  `PackingCollator` / `SequenceParallelCollator` keep pack / SP-pad / SP-slice,\r\n  flatten the `*_grid_thw_list` sidecars, record per-modality SP-pad patch counts,\r\n  and invoke the model hook after SP padding. No model-specific logic in the collator.\r\n- `mm_metadata.py` — shrunk to the genuinely generic helpers (`per_sample_metadata`,\r\n  `merge_position_id_returns`). The batch-level derivation moved to the model hooks.\r\n- `data_transform.py` — `_process_sample_qwen_vl_base` / `process_sample_qwen_omni`\r\n  propagate `rope_deltas` and emit `image_grid_thw_list` / `video_grid_thw_list`.\r\n- `trainer/base.py` + `dit_trainer.py` — `preforward` recurses into dicts so tensor\r\n  values inside `multimodal_metadata` land on the device.\r\n- `trainer/vlm_trainer.py` — `_build_collate_fn` resolves the two model hooks via\r\n  `getattr`; the former `model_type` hardcode for omni audio collate infos is gone.\r\n- `utils/helper.py` — `print_example` expands one level of nested dict.\r\n\r\n**Model integration (patchgen):**\r\n\r\n- Each wired `…ForConditionalGeneration` gains a `collate_multimodal_metadata`\r\n  patchgen helper + a `get_metadata_collate_func` override. Wired (gpu + npu where\r\n  present): `qwen3_vl`, `qwen3_vl_moe`, `qwen3_5`, `qwen3_5_moe`, `qwen3_omni_moe`.\r\n- `qwen3_omni_moe` Thinker.forward also consumes `rope_deltas`; omni models expose\r\n  `get_extra_collate_infos` for the audio feature tensors.\r\n- `qwen2_5_vl` / `qwen2_5_omni`: window-attention ViT (`cu_window_seqlens` from\r\n  `get_window_index`, config-dependent). These keep the in-forward derivation —\r\n  full integration is a tracked follow-up that needs GPU numeric verification.\r\n- All affected `generated/` files regenerated via patchgen.\r\n\r\n**Tests + docs:**\r\n\r\n- `tests/data/test_mm_metadata.py` — generic helpers, collator-hook handoff, hook\r\n  picklability.\r\n- `tests/models/test_model_forward_no_implicit_sync.py` — feeds synthetic\r\n  `multimodal_metadata` for the wired cases.\r\n- `.agents/knowledge/multimodal_metadata.md` — design doc.\r\n\r\n### Follow-up work (not in this PR)\r\n\r\n- Full `qwen2_5_vl` / `qwen2_5_omni` ViT integration (window-attention\r\n  `cu_window_seqlens` + `window_index` precompute).\r\n- Eliminate the remaining `get_rope_index` mrope syncs by precomputing mrope\r\n  `position_ids` collator-side.\r\n- The `dummy_forward` path (joint text-only + vision training) computes FA kwargs\r\n  in-forward and cannot use the collator precompute — needs its own handling.\r\n\r\n### Checklist Before Submitting\r\n\r\n- [x] Read the Contribute Guide\r\n- [x] Applied pre-commit checks\r\n- [x] Added/updated documentation (`.agents/knowledge/multimodal_metadata.md`)\r\n- [x] Added tests to CI workflow\r\n",
